Three contract tests pinning the SSOT guarantee end-to-end:
1. the same URL mints the SAME entity id from the full rebuild
   (build_application_model over crawled_data.surface_records) and the
   incremental apply_observation — verified against _endpoint_id_of
   itself, not a hardcoded string;
2. an incremental observation on top of a rebuild merges IN PLACE —
   no duplicate endpoint entity for the same tuple, revision bumped
   (A5b contract), and the method facet accumulates onto the merged
   entity;
3. double-apply of one observation is idempotent at the entity/relation
   level: identical entity set, identical relation set, refs merged
   (no duplicated evidence ref).

3/3 green on the A5a+A5b tree (evidence/A5c.txt). On 6f3dc7c the two
paths minted ids from two separate legacy sites — the equivalence is
now structural: one minter (_endpoint_id_of) for both.
